window.FIELD_CHAPTER_PARTS["book-1-full-book"][25] = "<p><strong>Online resources:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>ByteByteGo (Alex Xu's blog and YouTube). Visual system design. (<a href=\"https://bytebytego.com\">bytebytego.com</a>)</li>\n<li>High Scalability blog. Real architecture stories. (<a href=\"http://highscalability.com\">highscalability.com</a>)</li>\n<li>Patrick Collison's tech-aware curiosity. (<a href=\"https://patrickcollison.com\">patrickcollison.com</a>)</li>\n<li>Stripe's API design philosophy posts. (<a href=\"https://stripe.com/blog\">stripe.com/blog</a>)</li>\n<li>AWS / GCP / Azure architecture centers. Free reference architectures.</li>\n<li>OWASP. (<a href=\"https://owasp.org\">owasp.org</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tutorials and courses:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Database:</strong> Use the Mode SQL tutorial (Part 7). Then PostgreSQL official docs for depth.</li>\n<li><strong>APIs:</strong> Build a small project consuming Stripe's or Twilio's API. Read their docs.</li>\n<li><strong>Cloud:</strong> AWS Cloud Practitioner certification (free study materials).</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> OWASP top 10 walkthrough; Stanford's free CS155 lecture videos.</li>\n<li><strong>System design:</strong> ByteByteGo + system design mock interviews.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tools to learn:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Postman / Insomnia for API testing.</li>\n<li>DBeaver / TablePlus for database exploration.</li>\n<li>Chrome DevTools for web debugging.</li>\n<li>Sentry / Datadog for monitoring (read-only access).</li>\n<li>GitHub for code reading.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Write SQL daily on Mode, DataLemur, StrataScratch.</li>\n<li>Read 1 engineering blog post per week (Stripe, Uber, Netflix engineering blogs).</li>\n<li>Skim 1 PR per week from your eng team.</li>\n<li>Try one cloud service free tier per month.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p><em>End of Part 14. The next part is the soul of this book in many ways: how to come up with great product ideas and build them from zero.</em>\n-e</p>\n<p>\\newpage</p>\n";
